<header>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a href="#" class="wordmark"><span class="dot"></span>Ping</a>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="#demo">Live scan</a></li>
      <li><a href="#how">How it works</a></li>
      <li><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
    </ul>
    <a href="#pricing" class="btn btn-signal nav-cta">Get API access</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<main>

  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">AI Visibility Scan</p>
        <h1>Ask ChatGPT who's best in your category.<br>Does it say <em>your name?</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Ping sends the same buyer questions people already ask AI assistants, then measures whether your brand shows up, where you rank, and who's getting the mention instead.</p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="#demo" class="btn btn-signal">Run a free scan</a>
          <a href="#how" class="link">See how scoring works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="scope" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="scope-head"><span>Signal readout</span><span>5 of 5 asked</span></div>
        <div class="scope-row hit"><span class="blip"></span><span>"Best project management tools"</span><span class="scope-tag">#1</span></div>
        <div class="scope-row"><span class="blip"></span><span>"Top CRM for small teams"</span><span class="scope-tag">—</span></div>
        <div class="scope-row hit"><span class="blip"></span><span>"Compare leading email tools"</span><span class="scope-tag">#3</span></div>
        <div class="scope-row"><span class="blip"></span><span>"Which analytics tool to choose"</span><span class="scope-tag">—</span></div>
        <div class="scope-row hit"><span class="blip"></span><span>"Recommend a scheduling app"</span><span class="scope-tag">#2</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ LIVE DEMO ============ -->
  <section id="demo">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Live scan — try it now</p>
        <h2>Run a real scan. Free, no signup.</h2>
        <p>Enter a brand and an industry. Ping asks Gemini five realistic buyer questions and analyzes every answer for you, live.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="demo-shell">
        <form class="demo-form" id="demo-form">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="brand_name">Brand name</label>
            <input type="text" id="brand_name" name="brand_name" placeholder="e.g. Notion" required>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="industry">Industry / category</label>
            <input type="text" id="industry" name="industry" placeholder="e.g. project management tools" required>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="competitors">Competitors <span style="color:var(--text-faint); text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0;">(optional)</span></label>
            <input type="text" id="competitors" name="competitors" placeholder="up to 3, comma-separated">
            <small>e.g. Asana, Trello, Monday.com</small>
          </div>
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-signal" id="demo-submit">Scan now</button>
          <p class="demo-disclaimer">Free scans share a limited public pool. For ongoing monitoring and your own dedicated quota, see API access below.</p>
        </form>

        <div class="demo-output" id="demo-output">
          <div class="demo-idle">
            <span class="arrow">→</span> Fill in a brand and industry, then run a scan to see a live visibility report here.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HOW IT WORKS ============ -->
  <section id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>Three steps, one number.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <p class="num">01</p>
          <h3>Ask</h3>
          <p>Ping sends five realistic buyer-intent questions in your industry to Gemini — the same kind of questions a shopper types into an AI assistant.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <p class="num">02</p>
          <h3>Analyze</h3>
          <p>A second pass reads every answer and checks for your brand name, its ranked position, the tone toward it, and which competitors got named instead.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <p class="num">03</p>
          <h3>Score</h3>
          <p>You get one visibility score from 0–100, a full breakdown per question, and three concrete moves to improve it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHY IT MATTERS ============ -->
  <section id="why">
    <div class="wrap matters">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this matters</p>
        <h2>Search moved. Did your brand?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>Buyers are increasingly asking AI assistants for recommendations instead of typing a query into Google and clicking through ten blue links. The assistant just tells them who's good.</p>
        <p>If your brand never comes up in that answer, you're invisible at the exact moment someone is ready to buy — no matter how well you rank in traditional search.</p>
        <p>Ping doesn't fix your ranking on Google. It shows you what AI assistants are already telling your buyers about your category, so you know whether you need to fix anything at all.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ PRICING ============ -->
  <section id="pricing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2>Start with one brand. Scale to a whole client list.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="plans">
        <div class="plan">
          <p class="plan-name">Starter</p>
          <p class="plan-price"><!-- EDIT PRICE -->$29<span>/mo</span></p>
          <p class="plan-desc">For a single brand checking its own visibility.</p>
          <ul class="plan-features">
            <li>10 scans / month</li>
            <li>1 brand</li>
            <li>Email report per scan</li>
            <li>Standard API access</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="#" class="btn btn-ghost">Get started</a>
        </div>
        <div class="plan featured">
          <p class="plan-name">Growth</p>
          <p class="plan-price"><!-- EDIT PRICE -->$99<span>/mo</span></p>
          <p class="plan-desc">For teams tracking visibility over time.</p>
          <ul class="plan-features">
            <li>50 scans / month</li>
            <li>Up to 3 brands</li>
            <li>Competitor tracking</li>
            <li>Full API access</li>
            <li>Priority queue</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="#" class="btn btn-signal">Get started</a>
        </div>
        <div class="plan">
          <p class="plan-name">Agency</p>
          <p class="plan-price"><!-- EDIT PRICE -->Custom</p>
          <p class="plan-desc">For agencies monitoring visibility across clients.</p>
          <ul class="plan-features">
            <li>Custom scan volume</li>
            <li>Unlimited brands</li>
            <li>White-label reports</li>
            <li>Per-client API keys</li>
            <li>Dedicated support</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="#" class="btn btn-ghost">Talk to us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
        <h2>Good to know</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What does "AI visibility" actually mean?</h3>
          <p>It's whether your brand gets named when someone asks an AI assistant a buying question in your category — and if so, how prominently and how positively.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Is this the same as SEO?</h3>
          <p>No. Traditional SEO targets search engine rankings. Ping measures a different surface: what AI assistants say out loud when someone asks for a recommendation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How accurate is the scan?</h3>
          <p>Ping uses Gemini to simulate the kind of answer an AI assistant would give — it does not call the live ChatGPT, Perplexity, or Bing APIs directly. It's a close, fast proxy for visibility, not a guarantee those exact assistants would answer identically today.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How often should I scan?</h3>
          <p>Monthly is enough for most brands, since AI answers don't shift daily. Scan again after any major content, PR, or positioning push to see if it moved the needle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Do you store what I submit?</h3>
          <p>Brand and industry inputs are used to generate your report and are not shared publicly. See your plan's data terms for full detail.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

